KZ3 crash handler minidump (RSX pass 33): ppu_crash_report writes the minidump through kz3_log_write_minidump.

- Cause of the round-31/32 open item (nothing after MiniDumpWriteDump ran, exit 0xC0000005): patch 2030/2031 passed
  a hand-rolled `struct { DWORD tid; EXCEPTION_POINTERS* ep; BOOL client; }` as MINIDUMP_EXCEPTION_INFORMATION. The
  SDK declares that type 4-byte packed (ExceptionPointers at +4, size 16; MinGW's dbghelp.h agrees); the natural
  layout put the pointer at +8, so dbghelp read padding plus half a pointer (dbghelp!dump_exception_info+0x39:
  `mov rdx,[rax+4]; mov rcx,[rdx]`) and faulted on its own dump thread; the filter's once-guard let that second
  fault end the process. Reproduced without the game by tools/smoke/test_crash_dump.exe (variant "bug").
- Fix: kz3_log_write_minidump (port/kz3/kz3_log.c): the header's MINIDUMP_EXCEPTION_INFORMATION, dbghelp resolved
  at kz3_log_init, the dump written on a helper thread (Microsoft's guidance), result logged as [CRASH].
--- a/runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp
+++ b/runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp
@@ -3801,29 +3801,12 @@
                  g_active_ctx ? (uint32_t)g_active_ctx->cia : 0u, g_active_ctx ? (uint32_t)g_active_ctx->lr : 0u,
                  (unsigned long)GetCurrentThreadId());
         const char* crash = kz3_log_write_crash(reason, details);
-        if (crash && *crash) {
-            char dmp[600];
-            snprintf(dmp, sizeof dmp, "%s", crash);
-            char* dot = strrchr(dmp, '.');
-            if (dot && (size_t)(dot - dmp) + 5 < sizeof dmp) strcpy(dot, ".dmp");
-            /* KZ3 patch 2031: name the crash file before the minidump; the line after it never appeared in the
-             * round-31 test (the process ended with the exception code and a 14 kB dump: ASSUMPTION the dump
-             * call faults inside the handler), so the path must be on record before the attempt. */
-            fprintf(stderr, "[CRASH] crash file %s, writing minidump %s\n", crash, dmp);
-            fflush(stderr);
-            HANDLE f = CreateFileA(dmp, GENERIC_WRITE, 0, NULL, CREATE_ALWAYS, FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL, NULL);
-            if (f != INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE) {
-                typedef BOOL (WINAPI *mdw_fn)(HANDLE, DWORD, HANDLE, int, void*, void*, void*);
-                struct { DWORD tid; EXCEPTION_POINTERS* ep; BOOL client; } mei = { GetCurrentThreadId(), ep, FALSE };
-                HMODULE dh = LoadLibraryA("dbghelp.dll");
-                mdw_fn mdw = dh ? (mdw_fn)(void*)GetProcAddress(dh, "MiniDumpWriteDump") : NULL;
-                /* MiniDumpNormal (0): thread stacks and module list only; the 4 GB guest reservation stays out. */
